                        "entry_id": "3f167dee-0a80-3197-83be-96b9f4770d6d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The title of the leader, or patriarch, of the Ethiopian Orthodox Church."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0deb5bc-c9af-4dec-ba90-785f921d90e7",
                                "sense_id": "53532195-93a7-386a-84b3-dab9d4f55b93",
                                "text": "Two weeks later, before Abunas Pēṭros and Mātēwos, Menilek publicly swore not to deceive Mangashā nor cause him any harm."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b11429f5-b3aa-4038-80c6-1daeee7f7ac7",
                                "sense_id": "53532195-93a7-386a-84b3-dab9d4f55b93",
                                "text": "Thus, four Ethiopian monks were consecrated in Cairo in June 1929 (Abunas Abreham, Petros, Mikael, Yeshaq), and the fifth (Abuna Sawiros) was consecrated in Addis Ababa in January 1930."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
